       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects, and it isn't supported for any standard indication. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nPlease check whether one of these happened:\n- **Typo or unit error.** Did you mean 40 mg or 200 mg?\n- **Dose too high for the plan.** Typical dosing is 50 mg daily to start, and it's titrated in 25\u201350 mg steps to a usual range of 50\u2013200 mg/day.\n- **Intentional off-label dosing.** If your attending or psychiatry wants this, I can enter it with a note naming the prescriber and the rationale. Please confirm that first.\n\nTell me the dose you want, for example \"sertraline 50 mg PO once daily\" or \"200 mg PO once daily\", and I'll enter it right away. It's also worth running the plan by your senior or the pharmacist."
